Specifications
--------------

No specification or schema text is reproduced, and no specification
document or schema is redistributed. Element names, namespaces and
enumeration values are interface facts every implementation must use.

- OASIS Common Alerting Protocol Version 1.2 (and the CAP 1.1 and 1.0
  namespaces, read as 1.2) and its XML schema, copyright OASIS Open. The
  schema's content model is encoded as facts; the schema file is not
  included.
- OASIS EDXL Distribution Element 1.0 and 2.0, and the CAP v1.2 USA IPAWS
  Profile 1.0, copyright OASIS Open: names and rules used as facts.
- The Canadian Profile of CAP (CAP-CP) rule sets and event and location
  references, Public Safety Canada (Crown copyright): rules restated in
  our own words; the event codes are listed as values.
- US federal sources for IPAWS parameter values (47 CFR 11.31, National
  Weather Service CAP documentation, FEMA IPAWS-OPEN material): facts.
- W3C XML Signature Syntax and Processing, Atom (RFC 4287), RSS 2.0,
  GeoJSON (RFC 7946): used for facts only.

The India profile describes conventions observed in the public SACHET
feed of India's National Disaster Management Authority; it is not an
official profile and no NDMA or C-DOT text is reproduced.

